			},
			solution: {
				'index.html': `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{title}}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header" id="top">
      <p class="brand">{{name}}</p>
      <nav aria-label="Site sections">
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#sec-1">{{sections.0}}</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sec-2">{{sections.1}}</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sec-3">{{sections.2}}</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <h1>{{name}}</h1>
      <p>{{who}}</p>
      <p><a class="button" href="#inquiry">{{mainAction.label}}</a></p>

      <section id="sec-1">
        <h2>{{sections.0}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-2">
        <h2>{{sections.1}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="sec-3">
        <h2>{{sections.2}}</h2>
        <p>A couple of sentences about this section.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="offer">
        <h2>What we offer</h2>
        <div class="cards">
          {{#each items}}<article class="card">
            <h3>{{title}}</h3>
            <p>{{text}}</p>
            <p class="price">{{price}}</p>
          </article>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="inquiry">
        <h2>{{mainAction.label}}</h2>
        <form action="/inquiry" method="post">
          <p>
            <label for="f-name">What should we call you?</label><br>
            <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required>
          </p>
          <p>
            <label for="f-phone">Phone</label><br>
            <input id="f-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required>
          </p>
          <p><button type="submit">{{mainAction.label}}</button></p>
        </form>
      </section>
    </main>


    <section data-scaffold id="webhook-plan">
      <h2>Inquiry, webhook, owner</h2>
      <p id="channel">Channel: Slack. A message with the visitor’s name and phone number goes to the owner’s channel as soon as an inquiry reaches the handler. The fallback channel: an email.</p>
      <pre id="handler">import crypto from 'node:crypto';

const SECRET = process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET;   // the secret is in the environment, not in the code
const seen = new Set();                       // ids of events already processed

export async function handleWebhook(req, res) {
  const signature = req.headers['x-signature'];
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', SECRET).update(req.rawBody).digest('hex');
  const ok = signature && signature.length === expected.length &&
    crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(signature), Buffer.from(expected));
  if (!ok) return res.status(401).end();      // the signature does not match: not our service

  const event = JSON.parse(req.rawBody);
  if (seen.has(event.id)) return res.status(200).end();   // a repeat: already handled
  seen.add(event.id);

  await sendToOwner(event);                   // a message to the owner, for example via a Slack incoming webhook
  res.status(200).end();
}<\/pre>
      <p id="retry">If the receiver is down: the service retries the delivery after a minute, after an hour and later. The inquiry is not lost, because the handler is idempotent (a repeat with the same event id is ignored) and answers 200 quickly, while sending to the owner goes through a queue. If it stays down for long, I look at the delivery log.</p>
      <p id="graphql">GraphQL or REST for my data: for the list with “{{items.0.title}}” and the other items REST is enough, because the requests are simple and always the same. GraphQL would be handy if different screens needed different fields of the same data.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>{{name}}, {{city}}</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
`,
				'styles.css': `/* styles.css: the page after the CSS part, in short */

*,
*::before,
*::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

body {
  margin: 0;
  font: 1.0625rem/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  color: #1d2430;
  background-color: #ffffff;
}

main {
  max-width: 50rem;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
}

h1,
h2,
h3 {
  line-height: 1.2;
}

a {
  color: #1a4d8f;
}

nav ul {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.site-header {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
  padding: 1rem;
  color: #ffffff;
  background-color: #1a4d8f;
}

.site-header a {
  color: #ffffff;
}

.brand {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
}

.button {
  display: inline-block;
  min-height: 2.75rem;
  padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
  color: #ffffff;
  background-color: #1a4d8f;
  border-radius: 0.25rem;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.cards {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
  gap: 1rem;
}

.card {
  padding: 1rem;
  background-color: #f3f5f8;
  border-radius: 0.5rem;
}

.price {
  font-weight: 600;
}

input,
button {
  font: inherit;
}

